_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 11
---
order: 11
---
short_label: XIII.11
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If an equilateral pentagon is inscribed in a circle which has its diameter rational, then the side of the pentagon is the irrational straight line called minor.
----
proof:

In the circle {ABCDE|circT} which has its diameter rational let the equilateral pentagon {ABCDE|CDEAB} be inscribed.

I say that the side of the pentagon is the irrational straight line called minor.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="310" height="270" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="XIII.11 diagram" src="propXIII11.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Joyce's pentagon CDEAB is already faceless; the prose reaches it as
    // {ABCDE|CDEAB}. His circle circ has a random face, which a highlight
    // would raise over the pentagon (#140), so the prose reaches the circle
    // through circT, a faceless twin, as {ABCDE|circT}.
    //
    // His AG, BH, AC are held back until the construction sentence and drawn
    // there; his line N waits for "Let the square on N be equal to". The two
    // joins the proof makes in passing, AD and AH, are solid twins hidden at
    // rest (initiallyHidden), so the resting figure is unchanged.
    //
    // Transparent targets: the segments AF, FB, FK, BK, MK, MB, MF, CM, CL,
    // CD and the side AB; the triangles ACL, AMF, ABH, ABM (explicit ;0
    // faces); the circumferences ACG, ADG, ABC, AED, CG, GD as arcs. CG and
    // GD have no lettered point between their ends, so Xcg / Xgd
    // (uncoloured) are cut off on the ray from the centre F through each
    // chord's midpoint at the radius.
    //
    // Angle markers: the right angles at L (ALC, ALD) and at M (AMB, AMF) are
    // red squares pinned at 12 so the pairs sit side by side. LAC blue;
    // ACL = MFA green. Angle and triangle names collide (ACL, AMF): the
    // triangles own them, the angles take the display override.
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): C and D, free — the given
    // pentagon's base, standing from slide 1; N1, N4 (free, uncoloured,
    // off-canvas) and N2, the lineSlider end of N. N2 is deferred until N is
    // introduced. Every other point is derived and listed per slide.
    var GIVEN = ["circ","circT","CDEABdup","CDEAB","A","B","C","D","E","AB"];
    var CEN   = GIVEN.concat(["F"]);
    var DIAM  = CEN.concat(["AG","BH","G","H","AF","FB"]);
    var SETK  = DIAM.concat(["AC","K","FK","BK"]);
    var ARCS  = SETK.concat(["arcACG","arcADG","arcABC","arcAED","arcCG","arcGD"]);
